Manual follow-up patch: wire the Route Error Handling Check into
.github/workflows/ci.yml. See progress/task-20260718-065003-ai-engineering-
quality--error-handling.md, "Known limitation" section, for why this
couldn't be pushed directly in this PR (gh token lacks the `workflow`
OAuth scope).

Apply by inserting the block below into .github/workflows/ci.yml,
immediately after the `migration-collision-check:` job's
`- run: node scripts/check-migration-collision.mjs --base origin/main`
line and before the `doc-quarantine-banner:` job (i.e. as a new top-level
job at the same indentation as the other `jobs:` entries).

--- insert below this line ---
  route-error-handling-check:
    name: Route Error Handling Check
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v7
        with: { fetch-depth: 0 }
      # VERIDIAN Review Framework gap-closure (task-20260718-065003-
      # ai-engineering-quality--error-handling), [Low] Error Handling
      # Quality: "~9% of API routes lack a visible try/catch." Same
      # enforcement class as the coverage checks above -- fails the build
      # only on NEW or MODIFIED src/app/api/**/route.ts files (relative to
      # origin/main) that export an HTTP handler with no visible try/catch,
      # so pre-existing debt doesn't retroactively fail every PR. fetch-depth
      # 0 + --base origin/main, matching migration-collision-check's own
      # precedent just above (same "stale local main ref" fix). See the
      # script's own header for the honest limitation this does and doesn't
      # guarantee.
      - run: node scripts/check-route-error-handling.mjs --base origin/main
--- insert above this line ---

